# Finalise

When the user says `finalise`, `/finalise`, `fap`, `/fap`, `finalise-full`, `/ffap`, or `finalise and push`, run the matching npm script. Do not invent a manual test-commit-push handoff.

| User says | Command | Commit | Push |
|-----------|---------|--------|------|
| finalise / `/finalise` | `npm run finalise` | yes | no |
| fap / `/fap` / finalise and push | `npm run finalise:push` | yes | yes |
| finalise-full / `/finalise-full` | `npm run finalise:full` | yes | no |
| ffap / `/ffap` | `npm run finalise:full:push` | yes | yes |

- Contract: `iommarket-finalise-v1` in `scripts/finalise/trusted-actions.ts`
- Ordinary verify: `typecheck` + `test:run`
- Full verify: also `lint` + `build`
- Never apply Prisma/Supabase migrations or run `db:push` / `db:migrate` as part of finalise
- Repair only allowlisted failed steps with `npm run finalise:repair`, then rerun the original command once
- Never generically repair commit, push, database, or unknown steps
- State the branch and a short summary before any push
